    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e060a453_409b689a",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-13T06:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The abstract class here implies that in standard use case, user will need to @Override 3 callbacks every time they want to use the api instead of lambda expression.\nThus, is it possible that user wants to use named inherited class and use it everywhere to decrease complexity?\nE.g.\nclass MyXyzCallback extends InetAddresAnswerCallback\n\nIf yes, in the case of user wants to use MyXyzCallback,\nis it better if we:\n1. provide some info about the corresponding query when invoking callback? \nE.g. onQueryException(query, exception);\n2. provide basic empty callbacks in case user don\u0027t want to handle some of them?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40725c73_d56fd542",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-13T08:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good points.\n\nI don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to provide empty implementations of error callbacks, it will make it too easy to ignore errors.\n\nAs for passing in the query, I\u0027m not sure how we can do that given that we have two different query methods with two different signatures.\n\nEven if the user wants to use a named class, they don\u0027t have to use the same instance everywhere. The subclass can take a user-supplied tag in the constructor if desired:\n\n    resolver.query(\"www.google.com\", CLASS_IN, TYPE_AAAA, new MyXyzCallback(123));\n    resolver.query(\"www.googleapis.com\", CLASS_IN, TYPE_AAAA, new MyXyzCallback(456));",
      "parentUuid": "e060a453_409b689a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "825df1e0_4f294948",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-13T09:46:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it gives another reason of using a Builder.\nLike what we did in ka2.5 of socketKeepalive, if an object is used to bookkeeping all the information, and an indirect callback is used.\nThen we can give the information back to user, e.g.\n\nDnsQuery q \u003d DnsQueryBuilder.setDName(xyz).setType().setClass().build();\nq.query(new MyXyzCallback());\n\nclass DnsQuery {\n  void query(AnswerCallback answerCallback) {\n    mCallback \u003d new InternalCallback() {\n       @Override\n       void onQueryException(e) {\n           executor.execute(() -\u003e answerCallback.onQueryException(this, e));\n       }\n    };\n    \n    // do the query with the parameters we stored.\n    if(...)\n       resolver.queryVersion1(mDName, mClass, mType, ..., mCallback);\n    else\n       resolver.queryVersion2(..., mCallback);\n   }\n}\n\n\nI\u0027m not sure if this make sense.\nBut, yes, as you said, users can still manage it by having different instances.\nSo I don\u0027t have strong opinion about this.",
      "parentUuid": "40725c73_d56fd542",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7da1d2c1_8247709d",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T12:33:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find this very boilerplate-y. I would prefer a version like :\n\ninterface AnswerCallback\u003cQueryType, AnswerType\u003e {\n  public void onAnswer(@NonNull QueryType query, @NonNull AnswerType answer);\n}\n\npublic \u003cT\u003e void query(String query, ..., AnswerCallback\u003c? super String, T\u003e callback)\npublic \u003cT\u003e void query(byte[] query, ..., AnswerCallback\u003c? super byte[], T\u003e callback)\n\nThis reduces boilerplate and object allocation.",
      "parentUuid": "825df1e0_4f294948",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c31c420d_7f326cc6",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T12:35:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well I warmed up to the idea after all, in particular because my suggestion does not pass back the domain and type. Sure they are not often useful, but still. It\u0027s also more extensible.\nSo yes, let\u0027s go with this.",
      "parentUuid": "7da1d2c1_8247709d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd599867_0d825550",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T02:14:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Junyu\u0027s suggestion saves the allocation of a callback object, but requires the allocation of a query object. So it doesn\u0027t seem to result in a savings in code boilerplate or objects over what we have in this CL.\n\nFor it to be useful it also requires adding a DnsQuery class with getters and setters so that the parameters that were used in the original query can be retrieved from the query object. However, that\u0027s not trivial because if the user passes in a query blob, the getter for the hostname would have to parse the blob. That might not even be correct because for example the blob could have two hostnames in the question section, in which case the getter for the hostname would not be able to return a single string. So we can\u0027t just have the query only keep the blob and parse it on demand. We\u0027d have to keep the original parameters, and add a getter in the query object for each of the builder parameters.\n\nThat would be more complicated to implement and I don\u0027t think it buys us much in terms of ease of use. The user can always define an AnswerCallback subclass that takes in the constructor the parameters that they used to create the query. I think what we have in this CL right now is a good balance between API/implementation simplicity and ease of use.",
      "parentUuid": "c31c420d_7f326cc6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
