        "uuid": "168c038a_a786d8b0",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/DnsResolver.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T02:14:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think what you have now will throw ParseException if the user queries a name that does not exist, right? That\u0027s confusing. The response is perfectly valid, it\u0027s just that the name does not exist. In this case, I think it\u0027s better to call onAnswer with [] or null than to throw ParseException.\n\nWe should document this in the docstring for InetAddressCallback. Something like, \"If the answer does not contain any IP addresses, onAnswer will be called with an empty array\". (or \"will be called with null\").",
      "parentUuid": "c0fbeefa_9215171e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 312,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 312,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "c9f77bc4fd567a5d34f3e626cb5e112ec6b1df92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
